<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Worringen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1288</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-limburg-succession">War of the Limburg Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Worringen was fought on 5 June 1288 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-limburg-succession">War of the Limburg Succession</a>. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I of Brabant</a>, supported by the counts of Berg and Mark and by the citizens of Cologne, defeated Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegfried-of-westerburg">Siegfried of Westerburg</a> and his allies, capturing the archbishop. The archbishops could no longer rule the city, which became in effect free.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen.jpg" alt="Battle of Worringen" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Worringen_1288.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
